  "id": "acute-onset",
  "term": "acute onset",
  "definition": "Acute onset means symptoms begin suddenly and are severe from the start. In this packet, it refers to an abrupt appearance of problems such as obsessive-compulsive symptoms or restrictive eating, often along with clear changes in mood, behavior, and sensory or motor function.",
